{"term":"famine","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:c8895fe8829cd74a25","definition":"Extreme shortage of food in a region.","example":"It was reserved for Christians to torture bread, the staff of life, bread for which children in whole districts wail, bread, the gift of pasture to the poor, bread, for want of which thousands of our fellow beings annually perish by famine; it was reserved for Christians to torture the material of bread by fire, to create a chemical and maddening poison, burning up the brain and brutalizing the soul, and producing evils to humanity, in comparison of which, war, pestilence, and famine, cease to be evils.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["antifamine","famine bread","faminee","famine fever","famine food","famineless","faminelike","famine resistant","famine weed","feast or famine","famine or feast","nuclear famine","postfamine","prefamine","time famine"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/famine#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:30086826c6d49db7e5","definition":"A period of extreme shortage of food in a region.","example":"1986, United States Congress, House Select Committee on Hunger, Committee on Foreign Affairs, Subcommittee on Africa, Famine and Recovery in Africa\nThe root causes of the current famine are known: poverty, low health standards....","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":["antifamine","famine bread","faminee","famine fever","famine food","famineless","faminelike","famine resistant","famine weed","feast or famine","famine or feast","nuclear famine","postfamine","prefamine","time famine"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/famine#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kai